jobs.description:
Are you technically minded and looking for a full-time job in production? Then this position as an Operator in Nijmegen might be just right for you! As an operator, you are responsible for the proper functioning of various machines in the production process. You ensure that the production runs smoothly, you monitor quality, and you carry out small technical maintenance when necessary. Together with your team, you contribute to a clean and efficient working environment.

We expect an Operator to have the following background and skills:  - You work accurately and responsibly;
 - You are full-time available and live near Nijmegen;
 - You are fluent in English

 This in an entry level position, so everyone willing to work is welcome to apply. But because of the environment you'd be working in is a cleanroom, the selection will include an thorough estimation and evaluation of you ability to work in such an environment.

Are you looking for a challenging logistics position in a two-shift system? Do you want to work for the market leader in optical products? Then take a quick look at this vacancy! As a Logistics Employee in the two-shift system, you will be involved in every step of the logistics process. You ensure that incoming contact lenses are properly inspected, neatly sorted, and stored in the correct location in the warehouse. You will also be responsible for packing orders and making sure they are complete and shipped on time. You will be working in a two-shift system: from 7:00 AM to 3:30 PM and from 3:30 PM to 12:00 AM.

As a Logistics Employee in the two-shift system, you recognize yourself in the following job requirements:  - You are willing to work in a two-shift system;
 - You can work accurately in a calm and clean working environment;
 - You have experience in logistics;
 - You have a good command of Dutch and/or English.
